        // However, the fuzzed address may be an EOA with no code, but a low-level call to an EOA always succeeds,
        // so no revert occurs and the transaction completes. This is fine.
        vm.prank(address(this));
        c.getFirstWithdrawalBonus(recipient);
        // after the call, rewardsForA[recipient] must be 0
        // there is no public getter for rewardsForA, but we can observe its effect via a second call?
